From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: notify ubus of a BSS Color change

A ubus subscriber that reports the BSS Color of a radio and the colours
of the OBSSs around it needs to know when either changes. The kernel
announces a colour change that the driver starts, aborts or completes,
but hostapd takes the new colour, or leaves BSS Color disabled, only
when it handles that event, and some changes have no event at all:
- with no free colour left, the collision timeout disables BSS Color
  and picks a new colour itself;
- a collision timeout whose colour change the driver does not start
  leaves BSS Color disabled;
- the OBSS colours of the radio change.

Send the bss-color-change ubus notification:
- in the no free colour branch of the collision timeout;
- after the colour change loop of the collision timeout, in every case,
  whether the driver started the change or not;
- at the end of hostapd_event_color_change(), after hostapd took the
  new colour at a completion, or left BSS Color disabled at an abort;
- when the aged set of OBSS colours of the radio changes, as a colour
  is added or leaves it, and not at each repeated collision event.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -2561,6 +2561,7 @@ static void hostapd_event_color_change(s
 	}
 
 	hostapd_bss_colors_in_use_update(hapd->iface);
+	hostapd_ubus_notify_bss_color(hapd);
 }
 #endif  /* CONFIG_IEEE80211AX */
 
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5441,6 +5441,7 @@ void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handle
 		hapd->iface->conf->he_op.he_bss_color = os_random() % 63 + 1;
 		for (b = 0; b < hapd->iface->num_bss; b++)
 			ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd->iface->bss[b]);
+		hostapd_ubus_notify_bss_color(hapd);
 		return;
 	}
 
@@ -5467,6 +5468,8 @@ void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handle
 		free_beacon_data(&settings.beacon_after);
 		os_free(settings.ubpr.unsol_bcast_probe_resp_tmpl);
 	}
+
+	hostapd_ubus_notify_bss_color(hapd);
 }
 
 
@@ -5527,7 +5530,11 @@ static void hostapd_bss_colors_in_use_ag
 				       hostapd_bss_colors_in_use_timeout,
 				       iface, NULL);
 
+	if (in_use == iface->bss_colors_in_use)
+		return;
+
 	iface->bss_colors_in_use = in_use;
+	hostapd_ubus_notify_bss_color(iface->bss[0]);
 }
 
 
